       "description": {
        "short": "Riley Green and Hannah McFarland team up to “Go Again.”",
        "standard": "This playlist tracks what’s happening from the heart of the country scene to its outer edges. Find fan favorites you already love next to breakout stars and emerging voices. Topping the list this week is <b>Riley Green</b> with the <b>Hannah McFarland</b>collaboration “Go Again,” off Green’s just-released new album <i>That’s Just Me</i>. The duet is slow, sweet, and a little sexy, as Green and McFarland play new lovers saying goodbye the morning after a one-night stand.\n\nGreen made an effort to include a wide range of sounds on his new album. “I grew up in the era of burnt CDs and it would have 2pac and then Tim McGraw and then Merle Haggard,” he tells Apple Music. “I think that’s the way I like to do records.” Check back here early and often for updates, and if you hear something you like, add it to your library."
